load ../rule-autofail.maude

--- Coverage: a self-terminating workflow with an unhandled failed effect
--- reaches the failed terminal -- the workflow auto-fails instead of stalling.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  selfTerminating effFailedUnhandled(e1) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: a handled failure settles via its own terminal (the handler path
--- is reachable, so the model is not vacuously inert).
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  selfTerminating effFailedHandled(e1) running
  =>* settled(e1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: with one handled and one unhandled failure in the same
--- self-terminating workflow, the unhandled one still drives the auto-fail --
--- a settling sibling does not mask the unhandled failure.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  selfTerminating effFailedHandled(e1) effFailedUnhandled(e2) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: a service workflow records a durable diagnostic for the unhandled
--- failure AND stays running -- the diagnostic and running coexist.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  service effFailedUnhandled(e1) running
  =>* diagRecorded(e1) running RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (scope): without a scope marker, an unhandled failure never auto-fails.
--- The RESIDUAL soup var means an auto-fail in ANY reachable state would be a
--- solution, so No solution proves [autofail] requires the selfTerminating
--- marker rather than keying on any failed effect.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  effFailedUnhandled(e1) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (handled-ness): a handled failure in a self-terminating workflow never
--- auto-fails. If [autofail] keyed on any failed effect rather than only the
--- unhandled disposition this would find a solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  selfTerminating effFailedHandled(e1) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (all-handled): when every failure is handled, nothing auto-fails even
--- though the workflow is a terminal path.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  selfTerminating effFailedHandled(e1) effFailedHandled(e2) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (cancel exemption): a cancelled effect never trips the net -- cancel is
--- deliberate (the watchdog pattern), never an unhandled outcome. If the net
--- keyed on any non-success terminal this would find a solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  selfTerminating effCancelled(e1) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (service): a service workflow NEVER reaches instanceFailed, even with
--- an unhandled failure. If [autofail] matched the service scope this would
--- find a solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-RULE-AUTOFAIL :
  service effFailedUnhandled(e1) running
  =>* instanceFailed RESIDUAL:Cfg .
